  "limits": [
    "All claims concern byte-exact original retail DLL source instructions, metadata, call sites and branch targets, NOT successful game execution or DLC installation.",
    "SaveData.IsDLCInstalled is referenced twice; the input at the second call uses raw numeric DLC index 2 only when the original input equals raw numeric 3. DLC product-name labels and authored entitlement values are not established by this source.",
    "The story-specific branch compares raw numeric index 9 and touches StoryWork and StorySaveDataManager fields. Actual story-save contents, scenario outcome, and retail gameplay effects are NOT established.",
    "Both original helper methods are owned by DLCInitializer rather than DLCInstall. Their full bodies are identity-pinned by SHA only; interpreting their internal behavior requires separate source facts.",
    "The 13 switch cases and its default all branch to one common SaveData.dlcVersion[index] = 1 source operation; this is not proof that its memory write was executed or succeeded.",
    "Original Unity resources.assets parent SHA, actual retail-loaded fprwaza binding, and historical retail decoded asset vault remain unresolved; SOURCE_CONSOLIDATION_V1 viewer/runtime LOCKED."
